 "title": "Soils and Natural Vegetation of the World",
 "emoji": "🌱",
 "cards": [
  {
   "tag": "Why this matters",
   "h": "Soil and plants tie climate to people",
   "b": "<p>Soil decides what farmers can grow. Vegetation decides what animals and people can live there. Together with climate they give every region its character. UPSC asks for <b>distribution and reasons</b>: why laterite in the tropics, why chernozem in the steppes.</p>"
  },
  {
   "tag": "Core idea",
   "h": "Soil: how it forms",
   "b": "<p><b>Pedogenesis</b> depends on five factors: <b>parent material</b>, <b>climate</b>, <b>relief</b>, <b>organisms</b> and <b>time</b>. Climate is the most active. Warm, wet climates cause fast chemical weathering; cold or dry ones cause slow formation. Soil is a living system, 45% mineral, 25% water, 25% air and 5% organic matter, roughly.</p>"
  },
  {
   "tag": "Core idea",
   "h": "The soil profile",
   "b": "<svg class=\"d\" viewBox=\"0 0 320 174\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"6\" width=\"300\" height=\"26\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"160\" y=\"23\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">O horizon</text><text x=\"160\" y=\"38\" fill=\"#5d6474\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Leaf litter and humus</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"34\" width=\"300\" height=\"26\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f1e4c6\" stroke=\"#a8792a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"160\" y=\"51\" fill=\"#7d5a1c\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">A horizon: topsoil</text><text x=\"160\" y=\"66\" fill=\"#5d6474\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Dark, humus and minerals, roots</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"62\" width=\"300\" height=\"26\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#dceaec\" stroke=\"#2f6f7a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"160\" y=\"79\" fill=\"#2f6f7a\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">E horizon</text><text x=\"160\" y=\"94\" fill=\"#5d6474\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Leached zone (podzols)</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"90\" width=\"300\" height=\"26\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f4dcd5\" stroke=\"#a3362a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"160\" y=\"107\" fill=\"#a3362a\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">B horizon: subsoil</text><text x=\"160\" y=\"122\" fill=\"#5d6474\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Clay, iron and salts collect</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"118\" width=\"300\" height=\"26\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f1e4c6\" stroke=\"#a8792a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"160\" y=\"135\" fill=\"#7d5a1c\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">C horizon</text><text x=\"160\" y=\"150\" fill=\"#5d6474\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Weathered parent rock</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"146\" width=\"300\" height=\"26\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"160\" y=\"163\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">R: bedrock</text><text x=\"160\" y=\"178\" fill=\"#5d6474\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Unweathered rock</text></svg><p>A vertical cut through soil is a <b>profile</b>. The A horizon is the most fertile. <b>Leaching</b> washes nutrients down; <b>eluviation</b> and <b>illuviation</b> move clay and iron from upper layers to the B horizon.</p>"
  },
  {
