   "h": "Zonal soils of the world",
   "b": "<svg class=\"d\" viewBox=\"0 0 320 188\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"6\" width=\"80\" height=\"26\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f1e4c6\" stroke=\"#a8792a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"50.0\" y=\"23\" fill=\"#7d5a1c\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Soil</text><rect x=\"90\" y=\"6\" width=\"130\" height=\"26\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f1e4c6\" stroke=\"#a8792a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"155.0\" y=\"23\" fill=\"#7d5a1c\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Climate and place</text><rect x=\"220\" y=\"6\" width=\"90\" height=\"26\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f1e4c6\" stroke=\"#a8792a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"265.0\" y=\"23\" fill=\"#7d5a1c\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Note</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"32\" width=\"80\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"50.0\" y=\"51\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Laterite</text><rect x=\"90\" y=\"32\" width=\"130\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"155.0\" y=\"51\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Hot, wet tropics</text><rect x=\"220\" y=\"32\" width=\"90\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"265.0\" y=\"51\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Leached, red, poor</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"62\" width=\"80\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"50.0\" y=\"81\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Chernozem</text><rect x=\"90\" y=\"62\" width=\"130\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"155.0\" y=\"81\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Steppe, Ukraine, prairies</text><rect x=\"220\" y=\"62\" width=\"90\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"265.0\" y=\"81\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Rich, black, fertile</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"92\" width=\"80\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"50.0\" y=\"111\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Podzol</text><rect x=\"90\" y=\"92\" width=\"130\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"155.0\" y=\"111\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Taiga, cool wet</text><rect x=\"220\" y=\"92\" width=\"90\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"265.0\" y=\"111\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Acidic, grey, poor</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"122\" width=\"80\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"50.0\" y=\"141\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Desert soil</text><rect x=\"90\" y=\"122\" width=\"130\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"155.0\" y=\"141\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Dry, hot</text><rect x=\"220\" y=\"122\" width=\"90\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"265.0\" y=\"141\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Salty, low humus</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"152\" width=\"80\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"50.0\" y=\"171\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Tundra soil</text><rect x=\"90\" y=\"152\" width=\"130\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"155.0\" y=\"171\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Arctic</text><rect x=\"220\" y=\"152\" width=\"90\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"265.0\" y=\"171\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Frozen, thin</text></svg><p><b>Laterite</b> (Latin later, brick) forms by <b>laterisation</b>: silica leaches, iron and aluminium remain. Hardens on exposure, so it is used for bricks, as in Kerala and Karnataka.</p>"
  },
  {
   "tag": "Core idea",
   "h": "Natural vegetation: the biomes",
   "b": "<svg class=\"d\" viewBox=\"0 0 320 218\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"6\" width=\"90\" height=\"26\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f1e4c6\" stroke=\"#a8792a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"55.0\" y=\"23\" fill=\"#7d5a1c\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Biome</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"6\" width=\"100\" height=\"26\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f1e4c6\" stroke=\"#a8792a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"150.0\" y=\"23\" fill=\"#7d5a1c\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Climate</text><rect x=\"200\" y=\"6\" width=\"110\" height=\"26\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f1e4c6\" stroke=\"#a8792a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"255.0\" y=\"23\" fill=\"#7d5a1c\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Examples</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"32\" width=\"90\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"55.0\" y=\"51\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Rainforest</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"32\" width=\"100\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"150.0\" y=\"51\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Hot, wet</text><rect x=\"200\" y=\"32\" width=\"110\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"255.0\" y=\"51\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Amazon, Congo</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"62\" width=\"90\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"55.0\" y=\"81\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Savanna</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"62\" width=\"100\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"150.0\" y=\"81\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Hot, wet-dry</text><rect x=\"200\" y=\"62\" width=\"110\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"255.0\" y=\"81\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Africa, Brazil</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"92\" width=\"90\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"55.0\" y=\"111\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Mediterranean</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"92\" width=\"100\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"150.0\" y=\"111\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Dry summer</text><rect x=\"200\" y=\"92\" width=\"110\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"255.0\" y=\"111\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">California, Chile</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"122\" width=\"90\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"55.0\" y=\"141\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Temperate grass</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"122\" width=\"100\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"150.0\" y=\"141\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Semi-arid</text><rect x=\"200\" y=\"122\" width=\"110\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"255.0\" y=\"141\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Prairie, Steppe</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"152\" width=\"90\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"55.0\" y=\"171\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Taiga</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"152\" width=\"100\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"150.0\" y=\"171\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Cold</text><rect x=\"200\" y=\"152\" width=\"110\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"255.0\" y=\"171\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Siberia, Canada</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"182\" width=\"90\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"55.0\" y=\"201\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Tundra</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"182\" width=\"100\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"150.0\" y=\"201\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Polar</text><rect x=\"200\" y=\"182\" width=\"110\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"255.0\" y=\"201\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Arctic fringe</text></svg><p>Natural vegetation grows without human help. Temperature, moisture, soil and relief decide its type. With height, vegetation changes like it does with latitude: <b>altitudinal zonation</b>.</p>"
  },
  {
   "tag": "Core idea",
   "h": "Tropical and Mediterranean forests",
   "b": "<p><b>Equatorial rainforest</b>: evergreen, layered, rich in species. Hardwoods like mahogany and ebony, hard to harvest. <b>Monsoon forests</b> shed leaves in the dry season: teak, sal. <b>Savanna</b>: tall grass and scattered trees.</p><p><b>Mediterranean</b> vegetation has small, waxy, drought-proof leaves: olives, citrus and vines. These regions are the world's citrus and wine orchards, called \"orchards of the world\".</p>"
  },
  {
   "tag": "Core idea",
   "h": "Grasslands, taiga and tundra",
   "b": "<svg class=\"d\" viewBox=\"0 0 320 151\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"6\" width=\"100\" height=\"26\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f1e4c6\" stroke=\"#a8792a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"60.0\" y=\"23.0\" fill=\"#7d5a1c\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Prairies</text><rect x=\"116\" y=\"6\" width=\"194\" height=\"26\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"213.0\" y=\"23.0\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">North America</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"35\" width=\"100\" height=\"26\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#dceaec\" stroke=\"#2f6f7a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"60.0\" y=\"52.0\" fill=\"#2f6f7a\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Pampas</text><rect x=\"116\" y=\"35\" width=\"194\" height=\"26\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"213.0\" y=\"52.0\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Argentina</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"64\" width=\"100\" height=\"26\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f4dcd5\" stroke=\"#a3362a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"60.0\" y=\"81.0\" fill=\"#a3362a\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Veld</text><rect x=\"116\" y=\"64\" width=\"194\" height=\"26\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"213.0\" y=\"81.0\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">South Africa</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"93\" width=\"100\" height=\"26\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"60.0\" y=\"110.0\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Steppe</text><rect x=\"116\" y=\"93\" width=\"194\" height=\"26\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"213.0\" y=\"110.0\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Eurasia</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"122\" width=\"100\" height=\"26\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f1e4c6\" stroke=\"#a8792a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"60.0\" y=\"139.0\" fill=\"#7d5a1c\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Downs</text><rect x=\"116\" y=\"122\" width=\"194\" height=\"26\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"213.0\" y=\"139.0\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Australia</text></svg><p>Temperate grasslands are among the world's great wheat and cattle regions. <b>Taiga</b> is coniferous (pine, spruce, fir) with softwood for paper and matches. <b>Tundra</b> has mosses, lichens and dwarf shrubs on permafrost; reindeer are central to the ecosystem.</p>"
  },
  {
   "tag": "Debate",
   "h": "Is soil a renewable resource?",
   "b": "<p>Soil forms at a few centimetres per thousand years but erodes in decades if bare. Deforestation, over-grazing and chemical farming cause degradation and desertification. The UN Convention to Combat Desertification (<b>UNCCD</b>, 1994) works on this.</p><p>The debate: grow more food now, or protect the slow-forming soil base for the future? India's answer includes <b>Soil Health Cards</b> (2015) and watershed programmes.</p>"
  },
  {
   "tag": "Indian angle",
   "h": "India's soils and vegetation",
   "b": "<p>India's main soil types: alluvial, black (regur), red, laterite, arid and forest soils. Black soil comes from Deccan basalt and suits cotton. Laterite is in the Western Ghats and east coast.</p><p>Natural vegetation ranges from Western Ghats rainforest to Thar scrub and Himalayan alpine meadows (more in the Indian lessons). India lost some forest in the Himalaya and Northeast through jhum and mining, but the <b>Forest Survey of India</b> reports slow net gains in cover (as of ISFR 2023).</p>"
  },
  {
   "tag": "Exam lens",
   "cls": "exam",
   "h": "How to write this",
   "b": "<div class=\"box\"><h4>Likely questions</h4><p>\"Explain the process of laterisation and its effect on the soils of tropical regions.\" (10 marks)</p><p>\"Why are temperate grasslands called the granaries of the world?\" (10 marks)</p></div><p><b>Structure:</b> climate first, then soil, then vegetation, then human use.</p><p><b>Prelims tip:</b> match grasslands to their continents (pampas = Argentina, veld = South Africa, downs = Australia); chernozems are black earths of the steppe.</p>"
  }
 ],
